---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **「1세대·4세대·6세대」라는 선이 자료에 있나.** (`/generations`)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 오늘 씨앗(2026-09-08 스타뉴스): 「웃자고 시작한 게 진짜가 된 '6세대 걸그룹' 효리수」
 *   기사가 매일 쓰는 말인데 **그 경계를 어디서 가져왔는지 대는 곳이 없다.**
 *   우리는 380팀의 열람을 이미 갖고 있으니 그 선을 «시험할 수 있다».
 *
 * ⭐ 이슈+롱테일이다. 어느 팀이 「몇 세대」로 불리든 같은 표에 얹힌다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 하지 않는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 「몇 세대가 최고」라고 안 쓴다. 등수를 매기는 지면이 아니다
 * ⛔ 세대 경계를 «사실»로 내세우지 않는다 — 우리가 그은 선이고, 그것을 시험하는 것이 일이다
 * ⛔ 「6세대는 없다」고 안 쓴다. 우리 조건을 넘은 팀이 0 이라고만 쓴다
 * ⛔ 🔴 5세대 멤버몫 2.5% 를 「팀으로만 읽힌다」로 읽지 않는다.
 *    **멤버 문서가 아직 안 생긴 것**이다 — 문서가 쌓이는 데 걸리는 시간이지 팬의 행동이 아니다.
 *    이 함정은 화면에 «적어서» 손님이 속지 않게 한다
 * ⛔ 설립연도를 못 받은 72팀을 0 이나 「모름」 칸으로 안 채운다. 몇 팀인지 적는다
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-generation.json';

const TITLE = 'Do the K-pop generation labels show up in the reading?';
const 셈 = d.셈;
const 칸 = d.칸별.filter((c) => c.팀수 > 0);
const 빈칸 = d.칸별.filter((c) => c.팀수 === 0);
const 겹침줄 = d.이웃겹침.filter((x) => x.겹침 !== null);
const 시험 = d.경계시험;

/* ⭐ 지면이 «셀 때마다 다시 센다». 손으로 재고 적어 두면 자료가 바뀔 때 지면이 자기와 싸운다.
   어제 그것으로 두 지면이 틀린 수를 이고 살아 있었다(/peak-month · /fame-compare). */
const 겹침가장작은 = 겹침줄.length ? Math.min(...겹침줄.map((x) => x.겹침)) : null;
const 겹침가장큰 = 겹침줄.length ? Math.max(...겹침줄.map((x) => x.겹침)) : null;
const 큰뜀 = 시험 ? 시험.줄세운.slice(0, 8) : [];
const 경계뜀 = 시험 ? 시험.줄세운.filter((t) => t.경계인가) : [];
/* 경계가 «줄세운 것의 몇째»인가 — 「경계가 위쪽에 없다」를 수로 보이는 자리다 */
const 경계자리 = 시험
  ? 경계뜀.map((t) => ({ ...t, 자리: 시험.줄세운.findIndex((x) => x.해 === t.해) + 1 }))
  : [];

/* 🔴 5세대의 낮은 멤버몫이 «문서 나이»인지 보려면 멤버수를 함께 봐야 한다.
   멤버 문서가 한 명뿐인 팀이 섞여 있으면 그 몫은 팬 행동이 아니다. */
/* 🔴 [2026-09-08] 여기서 내가 틀렸다. 「5세대는 멤버 문서가 아직 없다」고 적었는데
   재 보니 5세대 멤버 문서가 «더 많았다»(중앙값 4 · 3세대 2). 문서는 있고 읽히지 않는다.
   ⛔ 그러니 까닭을 하나로 단정하지 않는다. 다섯 팀·열두 달로는 못 가른다 — 그 말을 화면에 적는다. */
const 본유닛만 = d.팀.filter((t) => !t.하위유닛짐작);
const 오세대본유닛 = 본유닛만.filter((t) => t.세대 === '5th').sort((a, b) => a.멤버몫 - b.멤버몫);
const 중앙 = (a) => { const v = [...a].filter(Number.isFinite).sort((x, y) => x - y); return v.length ? v[Math.floor(v.length / 2)] : null; };
const 오세대멤버문서중앙값 = 중앙(오세대본유닛.map((t) => t.멤버수));
const 삼세대멤버문서중앙값 = 중앙(본유닛만.filter((t) => t.세대 === '3rd').map((t) => t.멤버수));
const 오세대낮은수 = 오세대본유닛.filter((t) => Number(t.멤버몫) < 0.05).length;

const 수 = (n) => (n == null ? '—' : Math.round(Number(n)).toLocaleString('en-US'));
const 몫 = (v) => (v == null ? 'not measured' : `${(Number(v) * 100).toFixed(1)}%`);
/* ⭐ 겹침은 표와 본문이 «같은 꼴»이어야 한다 — 한 자리에 두고 둘이 이것만 쓴다 */
const 겹침꼴 = (v) => (v == null ? 'not measured' : `${Math.round(Number(v) * 100)}%`);
const 위키 = (t) => `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(String(t).split(' ').join('_'))}`;

/* 🔴 설명글의 수를 «손으로 적지 않는다». 어제 손으로 적은 수 둘이 지면에 살아 있었다 —
   자료가 바뀌면 설명글만 옛 수를 이고 남는다. 그래서 여기서 세서 만든다. */
const DESC =
  'The press sorts Korean acts into first through sixth generations. We put '
  + `${셈.본유닛팀수} acts against English Wikipedia reading and tested the lines: median `
  + 'reading climbs, but neighbouring generations overlap '
  + `${겹침꼴(겹침가장작은)} to ${겹침꼴(겹침가장큰)}, and the years reading actually breaks `
  + 'are not the years the labels break.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: d.열람창,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://query.wikidata.org/', 'https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} page="/generations" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Korean entertainment writing sorts groups into generations — first, second, third, and
    lately a sixth. The boundaries are quoted as if they were established, but no
    institution sets them and no database records them. They are a convention. So we did
    the one thing a convention allows: we took {수(셈.본유닛팀수)} Korean acts whose founding
    year we could verify, put them against how much they are read in English, and asked
    whether anything actually changes at the lines.
  </p>

  <p>
    Two things came out. Median reading does climb with each generation — that part holds.
    But the generations{' '}<b>overlap by {겹침꼴(겹침가장작은)} to {겹침꼴(겹침가장큰)}</b>, so knowing an
    act's generation tells you almost nothing about that act. And the years where reading
    genuinely breaks are{' '}<b>not</b>{' '}the years the labels put the break.
  </p>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Reading by generation</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Generation</th><th>Acts</th><th>Median reads</th>
          <th>Middle half runs</th><th>Median member share</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {칸.map((c) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{c.영문}</td>
            <td>{c.팀수}</td>
            <td>{수(c.통합열람중앙값)}</td>
            <td>{c.통합열람사분위 ? `${수(c.통합열람사분위.q1)} – ${수(c.통합열람사분위.q3)}` : 'not measured (under four acts)'}</td>
            <td>{몫(c.멤버몫중앙값)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Reads are the twelve months {d.열람창}, English Wikipedia, act page plus member pages
      added together. <b>Median, not average</b> — one act can be read a hundred times more
      than its neighbour, and an average would hand that act the whole generation.
      Suspected sub-units are held out of this table; {수(셈.하위유닛팀수)} of the
      {' '}{수(셈.이어붙인팀수)} acts we could date are sub-units, and they read like people
      rather than like groups because the sub-unit's own name is the part nobody knows.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The generations sit on top of each other</h2>
    <p>
      A median is a single point. What matters for any one act is the spread, so here is how
      much the middle half of each generation overlaps the middle half of the next.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Pair</th><th>Acts</th><th>Middle halves overlap</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {d.이웃겹침.map((x) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{x.가} → {x.나}</td>
            <td>{x.가팀수} · {x.나팀수}</td>
            <td>{겹침꼴(x.겹침)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Overlap is the shared part of the two middle-half ranges, divided by the narrower of
      the two. 100% means one generation's middle half sits entirely inside the other's.
      At these numbers the label is a description of when an act started, not a description
      of how much it is read.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where the reading actually breaks</h2>
    {시험 ? (
      <>
        <p>
          This is the test the labels have to pass. Line the acts up by founding year, and
          for each pair of consecutive years compare the median reading. If the generation
          boundaries are real, the biggest jumps should sit on them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Of the {시험.잰틈수} year-to-year gaps we could measure, {시험.잰경계수} are
          generation boundaries. Among the {시험.잰경계수} largest jumps,
          {' '}<b>{시험.위쪽에든경계수} {시험.위쪽에든경계수 === 1 ? 'is' : 'are'} a boundary</b>
          {' '}— chance alone would have given {시험.우연이면기대}.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Year begins</th><th>Median moves</th><th>Change</th><th>Acts either side</th><th>On a boundary?</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {큰뜀.map((t) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{t.해}</td>
                <td>{수(t.앞중앙값)} → {수(t.뒤중앙값)}</td>
                <td>{t.뜀}×</td>
                <td>{t.앞팀수} · {t.뒤팀수}</td>
                <td>{t.경계인가 ? 'yes' : '—'}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        {경계자리.length > 0 && (
          <p class="note">
            The boundaries we could measure land at position
            {' '}{경계자리.map((t) => `${t.자리} of ${시험.잰틈수} (${t.해}, ${t.뜀}×)`).join(' and ')}
            {' '}in that ranking. The two largest breaks are elsewhere:
            {' '}{큰뜀.slice(0, 2).map((t) => `${t.해} at ${t.뜀}×`).join(' and ')}. Both are a
            single year off a boundary, which is worth saying plainly — it is not evidence
            that nothing changed, it is evidence that the line is drawn a year from where the
            reading moves.
          </p>
        )}
        <p class="note">
          A gap is only counted when both years hold at least four acts, because a year with
          two acts in it moves on one act. {시험.잰틈수} of the year pairs cleared that;
          the rest are left out rather than filled in.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p class="note">
        Not measured — too few years hold enough acts to compare. We would rather say that
        than print a jump that rests on two acts.
      </p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The sixth generation is in print before it is in the data</h2>
    <p>
      {빈칸.length > 0 ? (
        <>
          Our set contains{' '}<b>no acts</b>{' '}in {빈칸.map((c) => c.영문).join(' or ')}. That is
          not a claim that no such groups exist — Korean outlets are naming them right now.
          It is a statement about what is measurable: an act founded in 2026 has had no
          twelve-month window to be read in, and English Wikipedia has usually not written
          it down yet. The label arrives first, the record arrives later, and for a while
          there is nothing to count.
        </>
      ) : (
        <>The newest generation has acts in our set; the counts are in the table above.</>
      )}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>🔴 A trap in the newest column, stated rather than hidden</h2>
    <p>
      In the first table the fifth generation's median member share is
      {' '}{몫(칸.find((c) => c.세대 === '5th')?.멤버몫중앙값)}, far below every older generation.
      Read carelessly that says fifth-generation fans care about the group and not the
      people. <b>It says nothing of the kind.</b>
    </p>
    <p>
      Our first explanation for it was wrong, and the correction is worth printing. We
      assumed the members had no English articles yet. They mostly do — the fifth-generation
      acts carry a median of {수(오세대멤버문서중앙값)} members with an article, against
      {' '}{수(삼세대멤버문서중앙값)} for the third generation. The articles exist. They are
      barely read.
    </p>
    <p>
      Here is the whole column, all {오세대본유닛.length} acts, so nothing hides behind a median.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Act</th><th>Founded</th><th>Members with an article</th><th>Member share</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {오세대본유닛.map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={위키(t.제목)} rel="nofollow">{t.이름}</a></td>
            <td>{t.데뷔해}</td>
            <td>{t.멤버수}</td>
            <td>{몫(t.멤버몫)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      {오세대낮은수} of the {오세대본유닛.length} send under 5% of their reading to members, and two
      have only one member with an article at all. Whether that is because the encyclopaedia
      has not caught up, or because attention on very new groups genuinely sits on the group
      name, <b>we cannot separate</b> — not with five acts and one twelve-month window. So we
      do not claim either. What we will not do is print {몫(칸.find((c) => c.세대 === '5th')?.멤버몫중앙값)}
      {' '}as a fact about fans of new groups.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    {d.이것이아닌것.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
    <p class="note">
      The boundaries in the first column are the ones Korean and English coverage tends to
      use. We wrote them into the collector so they can be read and argued with rather than
      inferred from our tables. If you would draw them elsewhere, the year-by-year gaps
      above are the part that does not depend on our lines.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where else this leads</h2>
    <p class="note">
      We measured a different thing on nearly the same acts and got the same shape:
      {' '}<a href="/group-afterlife">how long a group stays looked up after its peak</a>{' '}
      does not vary by debut era either — the median fall from a group's best month to half
      of it is about two months whether the group started in 1995 or 2020. Two separate
      measurements, both finding that the era an act belongs to explains less than the label
      implies. And for where a group's reading lands once you have it,
      {' '}<a href="/member-vs-group">the group page or the member pages</a>{' '}is the split
      this page reuses.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/generations" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Founding years — Wikidata SPARQL, property P571 <i>inception</i>. Where an act carries
      several, the earliest is used. Of {수(셈.앞자료팀수)} acts,
      {' '}{수(셈.설립연도받은팀수)} had a usable year and{' '}{수(셈.뺀팀수)}{' '}did not; the
      {' '}{수(셈.뺀팀수)}{' '}are left out of every table rather than placed in an
      "unknown" row. Founding year is not always debut year — some acts trained for years
      before releasing — and we do not have release dates for all of them.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Reads — Wikimedia Pageviews REST API, English Wikipedia, all-access,
      {' '}<b>agent=user</b>{' '}(bots excluded), monthly, {d.열람창}. The current month is
      excluded because it is not finished. Reading was not re-collected for this page; it is
      the same measurement as{' '}<a href="/member-vs-group">/member-vs-group</a>, joined by
      Wikidata identifier. Counted {d.잰때}.
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
